<title>USA: Normal temps expected in Brazil coffee belt - WSC.</title>
<headline>Normal temps expected in Brazil coffee belt - WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Low pressure expected to intensify off the coast of Buenos Aires this weekend should remain too far to the south of Brazil's coffee belt to bring back any cold weather to the area, Weather Services Corp said in an update on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Fair to partly cloudy skies were observed this morning while temperatures were near normal. Low temperatures ranged 45-55 F (7-13 C).</p>
<p>The outlook calls for partly to variably cloudy skies during the next 5-7 days with the chance of a few light showers developing. Temperatures should remain near normal levels with lows in the 50s F (low to middle teens C).</p>
<p>There is no damaging cold expected, according to WSC.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212 859-1640))</p>
</text>
